Data
----
civic-link stores no data snapshot. It queries CIViC (Clinical Interpretation of Variants
in Cancer, https://civicdb.org, Griffith Lab, Washington University School of Medicine)
live over its public GraphQL API (https://civicdb.org/api/graphql) and the nightly variant
summary download on the same host. CIViC content is released under the Creative Commons
Public Domain Dedication (CC0 1.0 Universal); the CIViC application source code is MIT
licensed. No permission is required, but please attribute CIViC and cite:

  Griffith M, Spies NC, Krysiak K, et al. CIViC is a community knowledgebase for expert
  crowdsourcing the clinical interpretation of variants in cancer. Nat Genet.
  2017;49(2):170-174. PMID: 28138153.

  Krysiak K, Danos AM, Saliba J, et al. CIViCdb 2022: evolution of an open-access cancer
  variant interpretation knowledgebase. Nucleic Acids Res. 2023;51(D1):D1230-D1241.
  PMID: 36373660.

Research use only. Not for clinical decision support, diagnosis or treatment. The output
of this server is not a clinical actionability report: CIViC is a community-curated
knowledgebase, and absence of CIViC evidence is not evidence that a variant is not
actionable or not oncogenic.
